# JSON.stringify of an object with a proven layout does not start with the built-in. A string builder is taken from the pool by two loads and two stores.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="write" role=Source
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#0:
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[pooled]] = Load(b@{{*}}, offset = {{*}}, ControlDependent|Reads:collectorState, {{*}}:StringBuilderBegin)
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[pooled]], Terminal, {{*}}:StringBuilderBegin)
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:#{{*}}, Else:Rare:#
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[next]] = Load(b@[[pooled]], offset = {{*}}, ControlDependent|Reads:AOTStringBuilderStorage_fields, {{*}}:StringBuilderBegin)
# CHECK-NEXT: Store(b@[[next]], b@{{*}}, offset = {{*}}, ControlDependent|Writes:collectorState, {{*}}:StringBuilderBegin)
# The writer that was compiled for the layout is called directly with the object and the builder, and says whether it could write all of it.
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[written]] = Patchpoint(b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), b@[[builder]]:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), ExitsSideways{{*}}:CallDirect)
# CHECK: Int32 b@{{*}} = Equal(b@[[written]], $1(b@{{*}}))
# One more call makes the string out of the builder.
# CHECK: Int64 b@{{*}} = Patchpoint(b@[[builder]]:Register({{*}}), {{*}}, resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), ExitsSideways{{*}}:StringBuilderFinish)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# The writer and the built-in are each called at one place, the built-in behind a rare edge, for an object that the writer gave up on.
# CALLS-LABEL: name="write" role=Source
# CALLS-COUNT-1: ExitsSideways{{*}}:CallDirect)
# CALLS-NOT: = Patchpoint({{*}}:CallDirect)
# CALLS: Successors: Then:Rare:#[[itself]], Else:#
# CALLS: BB#[[itself]]:
# CALLS-COUNT-1: ExitsSideways{{*}}:CallBuiltin)
# CALLS-NOT: ExitsSideways{{*}}:CallBuiltin)
# CALLS-LABEL: end of function
# The counts hold calls, whose moves follow the calling convention: not for Windows.
# X64: instructions: 31, patchpoints: 2, rare instructions: 15
# ARM64: instructions: 34, patchpoints: 2, rare instructions: 16
